-- Ecuador deep-dive content (English). Ecuador's story is a genuine,
-- mature Americas clearance-model mandate -- near-real-time transmission
-- since 2014, not a January 2026 introduction of real-time reporting.
-- Live-researched via direct reads of SRI's own resolution PDFs
-- (sri.gob.ec, including NAC-DGERCGC14-00790, NAC-DGERCGC18-00000233,
-- NAC-DGERCGC24-00000022, NAC-DGERCGC24-00000035, NAC-DGERCGC25-00000014,
-- NAC-DGERCGC25-00000017) plus Primicias, El Comercio, AVL Abogados,
-- Sovos, and EDICOM. mandate_summary and timeline_intro deliberately
-- kept short (per the lesson of migration 355).
--
-- CRITICAL FRAMING: January 2026's headline change is the closure of a
-- temporary 4-business-day grace period granted in November 2024 during
-- Ecuador's electrical-emergency crisis, NOT the introduction of
-- real-time reporting -- Ecuador's SRI has required near-real-time
-- transmission since 2014. This framing is baked into timeline_intro,
-- the scope_transmission "Transmission-window history" card, and the
-- ec-realtime-transmission-2026 milestone (migration 379).
--
-- Technical/compliance-model hedge: Ecuador is best described as a
-- clearance-style CTC model with self-computed authorization keys.
-- Secondary sources disagree on the exact sequencing (SRI-approves-first
-- vs. deliver-immediately-with-parallel-authorization) -- hedged
-- explicitly in the first file_format card's note rather than asserted
-- as settled fact.
--
-- RIMPE Negocios Populares carve-out (income <= $20,000, exempt, may use
-- paper "notas de venta RISE") is noted in the scope card, a penalties
-- card, and the mandate_summary/scope_intro text -- not literally every
-- taxpayer is in scope.









